&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ethos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethos (Nasdaq: $LIFE) &lt;/strong&gt;is a leading life insurance technology company on a mission to protect families by democratizing access to life insurance and empowering agents at scale. With its robust three-sided technology platform, Ethos is transforming the life insurance experience for consumers, agents, and carriers alike. Ethos offers instant, accessible products and a seamless online process that requires no medical exams and just a few health questions; it eliminates traditional barriers, making it easier than ever for everyone to protect their families. Ethos is redefining how life insurance is bought, sold, and underwritten.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Operations builds the connective tissue between product and user-facing teams so Ethos can ultimately deliver more value to more users, faster. As a Product Operations Analyst, you’ll work cross-functionally with both customer-facing teams and product and engineering teams to ensure a seamless customer experience. You&#39;ll play a key role in strengthening the feedback loop between the field and our product teams, helping surface and resolve issues efficiently. This is a high-impact individual contributor role that is essential to delivering on our mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage and investigate technical and product issues raised by customer-facing teams using backend tools and data platforms like Datadog, FullStory, Amplitude, and Snowflake&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a product quality advocate by fielding feature requests, triaging surfaced issues, and partnering with engineers and product managers to identify, scope, and resolve bugs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary liaison between product/engineering and customer-facing teams, clearly communicating product updates and issue resolutions to relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
