&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ethos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethos (Nasdaq: $LIFE) &lt;/strong&gt;is a leading life insurance technology company on a mission to protect families by democratizing access to life insurance and empowering agents at scale. With its robust three-sided technology platform, Ethos is transforming the life insurance experience for consumers, agents, and carriers alike. Ethos offers instant, accessible products and a seamless online process that requires no medical exams and just a few health questions; it eliminates traditional barriers, making it easier than ever for everyone to protect their families. Ethos is redefining how life insurance is bought, sold, and underwritten.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ethos is building a People organization that scales through both talent and technology, and this role sets the direction for how we get there. As Director, Global People Operations &amp;amp; AI, you&#39;ll own how People services are delivered worldwide: the Global People Services team, the operating model that supports every employee, and the automation and enablement strategy for the entire People organization. You&#39;ll define and stand up a tiered service model that moves work fluidly from self-service, to shared services, to experts, and you&#39;ll set the vision for where AI agents and automation handle repeatable work so our people can focus on judgment, complexity, and experience. You&#39;ll lead a growing team, partner with HR Technology, IT, Legal, and People leaders across regions, and build the governance and controls that let us scale responsibly. This is a strategic, hands-on leadership role for someone who can design an operating model and then make it real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy and multi-year roadmap for Global People Operations, defining how the People organization delivers services across all regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Global People Services team, setting standards, service levels, quality, and coverage across geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the direction for automation and enablement across the global People organization, establishing an operating model where AI agents and automation carry repeatable work and people own judgment and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement a tiered service model spanning self-service (knowledge, portals, and AI assistants), shared services (People Ops handling routine and mid-complexity cases), and experts (centers of excellence and senior partners for complex work), with clear routing and escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the governance framework for AI and automation in People Ops: guardrails, human-in-the-loop controls, privacy, security, auditability, and compliance across jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the metrics that measure success: service levels, case deflection, cycle time, cost-to-serve, accuracy, and employee experience, reporting outcomes to leadership and using them to prioritize investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and coach the People Operations team, including the People Product Managers, building capability in process design, agent oversight, and service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with HR Technology, IT, Legal, Finance, and People leaders to align global systems, data, and processes, and to advance operations through automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own change management and adoption for new processes, automations, and the tiered service model across regions and cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure global compliance and data governance across the markets where Ethos operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendors, budget, and the tooling roadmap for People Operations and shared services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously scale and improve the operating model as Ethos grows and enters new markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in People/HR Operations, shared services, or people/business operations, including several years leading teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building or running a People/HR shared services function and a tiered service model (self-service, shared services, experts).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record setting automation and enablement strategy and deploying AI or agentic solutions in an operations context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operating discipline: service-level management, metrics, cost-to-serve, and capacity planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating globally across multiple countries, with a working knowledge of regional compliance and data-privacy requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership, stakeholder-management, and executive communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of AI governance: privacy, fairness, security, auditability, and human oversight designed-in from the start.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change-management expertise, with the ability to drive adoption at scale across a distributed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment in handling sensitive, confidential, and high-stakes situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree required; relevant certifications preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
