&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ethos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethos (Nasdaq: $LIFE) &lt;/strong&gt;is a leading life insurance technology company on a mission to protect families by democratizing access to life insurance and empowering agents at scale. With its robust three-sided technology platform, Ethos is transforming the life insurance experience for consumers, agents, and carriers alike. Ethos offers instant, accessible products and a seamless online process that requires no medical exams and just a few health questions; it eliminates traditional barriers, making it easier than ever for everyone to protect their families. Ethos is redefining how life insurance is bought, sold, and underwritten.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Director of Product Design to lead and elevate design for Ethos’s Partnerships business and Platform teams.Buying life insurance is one of the most important financial decisions a family can make. The vast majority of families complete this purchase with the facilitation of an agent. For the last hundred years this process was dominated by paper-heavy, multi-week purchase flows that made selling and buying life insurance a pain. Today, Ethos is giving them modern digital tooling to transform that. Ethos’s Partnerships Business is our B2B2C channel that gives independent insurance agents and insurance agencies a digital-first platform, automated underwriting infrastructure, and multiple insurance offerings that help them serve their clients faster and grow their business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;As the head of design for Ethos’ Partnership and Platforms you will have a direct opportunity to shape how design helps agents and their customers achieve their goals. This is a role with broad surface area and ideal for someone with the interest and versatility to work across a wide range of domains including agent onboarding and activation, quoting, applications, and sales, agent growth and retention, compensation, enterprise/agency management, partner integrations, insurance product expansion, underwriting, payments and more — all of which have direct or indirect impact on the end-customer experience.&lt;br&gt;This role combines an eye for craft, strategic vision, team management, with hands-on design and product building excellence. You’ll champion intentional, intuitive, and strategic product experiences, compelling storytelling, and measurable business impact — and will help make Ethos the most trusted and user-friendly life insurance experience in the world for agents and their clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead design for Partnerships and Platform&lt;/strong&gt; — covering agent onboarding and activation, quoting, applications, and sales, agent growth and retention, compensation, enterprise/agency management, partner integrations, insurance product expansion, underwriting, payments experiments, and more. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead, mentor, and grow a small but mighty team of product designers. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work closely with Research to discover and prioritize meaningful opportunities that improve business outcomes and agent success &lt;/strong&gt;— collaborating with Product and Leadership to shape roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work crossfunctionally with Marketing, Lifecycle Marketing, Performance Creative and Brand to shape compelling and connected end-to-end journeys for agents and agencies and their clients across segments, needs and products. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to create an environment of excellence and growth &lt;/strong&gt;where team members can do their best work and grow professionally and personally. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as Design Site Leader for Ethos India&lt;/strong&gt; — Raise the bar for the design practice globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product design (UX) experience, including several years leading multi-person design teams.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of start-up experience requiring fast decision making and ability to evaluate ambiguous product problems with a mix of intuition, user experience, and measurement.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on B2B2C, gig economy, and products serving a range of company sizes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to design for &lt;strong&gt;complex, decision-heavy user journeys&lt;/strong&gt; in industries like fintech, healthtech, or insuretech.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of &lt;strong&gt;conversion optimization&lt;/strong&gt;, user motivation, and behavior design principles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and lead high performing teams. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio showcasing strong visual, interaction design, and storytelling craft alongside compelling impact delivered for past businesses and their customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
