&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ethos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethos (Nasdaq: $LIFE) &lt;/strong&gt;is a leading life insurance technology company on a mission to protect families by democratizing access to life insurance and empowering agents at scale. With its robust three-sided technology platform, Ethos is transforming the life insurance experience for consumers, agents, and carriers alike. Ethos offers instant, accessible products and a seamless online process that requires no medical exams and just a few health questions; it eliminates traditional barriers, making it easier than ever for everyone to protect their families. Ethos is redefining how life insurance is bought, sold, and underwritten.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Support is the front line for resolving escalated issues that reach our internal teams and customers - the layer between day-to-day support and deep technical investigation. As a Product Support Associate, you&#39;ll own escalated cases end to end: diagnosing what&#39;s actually going wrong, resolving it directly when you can, and looping in engineering or product only when a case genuinely requires deeper investigation. Most cases you&#39;ll handle are resolvable with the right systems knowledge and a sharp eye for detail - this role is about speed, accuracy, and follow-through.This is a high-impact individual contributor role for someone who thrives on solving problems for people, is relentless about getting to the right answer, and wants to build the operating rhythm of a brand-new team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own escalation cases end to end - triaging incoming issues from internal teams and customers, diagnosing root cause, and resolving them directly whenever possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accuracy and clarity in every resolution: small errors here have outsized downstream impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build fluency across the systems that matter for troubleshooting and backend tools (e.g., Datadog, Amplitude) to recognize when something is a known issue vs. something new&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a clear, responsive point of contact for the internal teams and customers who filed the case, keeping them updated and setting accurate expectations on timing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get on the phone with customers when a case calls for it, walking them through a solution or troubleshooting live rather than relying solely on written back-and-forth .While not all escalations will require customer interaction, this team will regularly be working with customers to ensure solutions are found through a good customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet defined service levels for response and resolution time, and hold yourself accountable to individual and team goals as the team&#39;s cadence gets established.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and recognize patterns when the same issue shows up repeatedly, flag it as a candidate for a permanent fix rather than a one-off resolution, and help build the internal knowledge base so recurring issues get faster to resolve over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3 years of experience in customer support, technical support, operations, or a related troubleshooting role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in Salesforce or equivalent case management/help desk software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical instincts and technical curiosity - you can navigate unfamiliar systems and figure out what&#39;s actually happening without needing everything explained&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to explain a resolution clearly to both a frustrated customer and an internal stakeholder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized, with a strong sense of ownership over open cases and follow-through on commitments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
