&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ethos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethos (Nasdaq: $LIFE) &lt;/strong&gt;is a leading life insurance technology company on a mission to protect families by democratizing access to life insurance and empowering agents at scale. With its robust three-sided technology platform, Ethos is transforming the life insurance experience for consumers, agents, and carriers alike. Ethos offers instant, accessible products and a seamless online process that requires no medical exams and just a few health questions; it eliminates traditional barriers, making it easier than ever for everyone to protect their families. Ethos is redefining how life insurance is bought, sold, and underwritten.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ethos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Ethos makes life insurance simple to buy, through our own platform and through agent and partner channels. Salesforce supports our sales, customer experience, and partnership teams as they grow. We are looking for a Salesforce Developer to build and support the custom applications and integrations these teams depend on, from design through deployment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;You will design, build, and support applications and integrations on Salesforce. This is full-lifecycle work: requirements, design, build, test, deploy, and support. We work source-driven and Git-based, and we release through automated pipelines instead of large quarterly releases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll work with Salesforce Administrators, business analysts, data engineers, and product engineering teams, as part of the Enterprise Systems team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Event integrations. Customer and policy events from our product platform update Salesforce in near real time and sync out to our sales and marketing systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Partner APIs. APIs that partners and internal services use to manage agent and partner data in Salesforce.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Consent and compliance. Contact preferences and Do-Not-Contact requests that must stay consistent across our communication systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Sales and service tooling. Apps, automation, and routing for our sales agents and service teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Build reliable event-driven integrations. Handle duplicate and late events, recover from failures, and give support teams clear diagnostics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Build and maintain inbound REST APIs and outbound callouts to external systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Build and improve Apex, LWC, and Flow solutions. Maintain existing automation, and move logic to Apex when scale, control, or testing needs require it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Write Apex that works at volume. Bulkify every path and design around governor limits, record locks, and async job limits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Protect personal and health data. Enforce appropriate sharing, object and field access, and least privilege. Choose execution context explicitly, document privileged integration operations, and keep sensitive data out of logs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Build integrations with Named and External Credentials, OAuth 2.0, Platform Events, Change Data Capture, and Apex REST. Design for retries, idempotency, and partial failure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Write tests that check behavior and failure cases. Use mocks where appropriate, address static-analysis findings, and review code from teammates, contractors, and AI tools.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Deploy through Git-based CI/CD. Manage sandboxes, destructive changes, rollback plans, and the three annual Salesforce releases. Keep Git and production in sync.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Support what we&#39;ve shipped. Triage production issues, debug across integration boundaries, and fix root causes instead of symptoms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Typically 5+ years of Salesforce development experience, not admin and config work alone, or equivalent evidence of delivering and supporting production systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Strong Apex, SOQL, bulk processing, asynchronous processing, and automated testing skills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience building REST or event-driven integrations that handle duplicate messages, retries, and partial failures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Ability to build and debug Flow and LWC (modern JavaScript, ES6+) solutions, and explain when Apex is the better choice.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with Salesforce data models, sharing, object and field access, Salesforce CLI, Git, and automated deployments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Ability to investigate production failures, review code, and explain technical decisions to business teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;You use the team&#39;s AI coding tools and check their output for correctness, security, and maintainability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with trigger frameworks and layered Apex design (domain, selector, and service classes), dependency injection, and mocking libraries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience integrating Salesforce with customer data platforms, contact-center systems, marketing tools, or identity providers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Insurance or financial services experience, especially with agent or partner distribution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Consent and privacy compliance (TCPA, CCPA).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Salesforce Platform Developer II certification.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Salesforce Sales Cloud and Service Cloud, Apex, LWC, Flow, Platform Events, and Change Data Capture. Integrations with customer data, contact-center, marketing, and identity platforms. GitHub with automated CI/CD. Snowflake as our warehouse. Slack for collaboration and alerting. Jira for tracking.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;The US national base salary range for this full-time position is $96,000 - $169,000. Our salary ranges are determined by role, level, and location. The range displayed on each job posting reflects the minimum and maximum target for new hire salaries for the position across all US locations. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only and do not include applicable bonus, equity, or benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;You can find further details of our US benefits at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ethoslife.com/careers/&quot;&gt;https://www.ethoslife.com/careers/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t meet every single requirement? If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. At Ethos we are dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive and authentic workplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. Pursuant to the SF Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider employment for qualified applicants with arrests and conviction records.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about what information we collect and how it may be used, please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://res.cloudinary.com/getethos/image/upload/v1684458868/00_CMS/CURRENT_CRPA_Privacy_Notice_for_Job_Applicants_05-23.docx_-_Google_Docs_lr4j43.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://res.cloudinary.com/getethos/image/upload/v1684458868/00_CMS/CURRENT_CRPA_Privacy_Notice_for_Job_Applicants_05-23.docx_-_Google_Docs_lr4j43.pdf&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1684616836493000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw2BlajerdOWoHawb8unUdI4&quot;&gt;California Candidate&amp;nbsp;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
