&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ethos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethos (Nasdaq: $LIFE) &lt;/strong&gt;is a leading life insurance technology company on a mission to protect families by democratizing access to life insurance and empowering agents at scale. With its robust three-sided technology platform, Ethos is transforming the life insurance experience for consumers, agents, and carriers alike. Ethos offers instant, accessible products and a seamless online process that requires no medical exams and just a few health questions; it eliminates traditional barriers, making it easier than ever for everyone to protect their families. Ethos is redefining how life insurance is bought, sold, and underwritten.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ethos has digitized one of the most painful journeys in consumer finance. Today, someone can apply for life insurance in minutes, with no medical exam and just a few health questions. Our digital experience is highly functional; now we want to make it inspirational, educational, and genuinely helpful at the moments that matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an exceptional Product leader to own the back half of our consumer funnel: the health interview where users answer sensitive questions and get an instant underwriting decision and the post-approval experience where they choose how much coverage they need, for how long, and complete their purchase. These are the highest-stakes moments in the journey, where trust, clarity, and confidence determine whether a family ends up protected. Your work will have a direct and positive impact on people’s lives at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for a senior product leader who pairs first-principles thinking and deep consumer empathy with rigorous experimentation and a talent for simplifying complexity. Ethos is a product-first company, and Product leaders (as well as PMs) here operate with a high degree of ownership.You&#39;ll lead a team of product managers, set the multi-year vision for these surfaces, drive your team’s quarterly planning and roadmap, and be accountable for results at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; People Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and grow a team of product managers, building a culture of ownership, rigorous experimentation, and shared learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear goals and development plans for your team, run regular performance conversations, and raise the bar on PM craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with recruiting to hire exceptional PMs as the team scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay hands-on: go deep with your PMs and cross-functional team to give them the steering, feedback, and unblocking they need to excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy &amp;amp; Vision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product vision and roadmap for the application and purchase experience, from the start of the health interview through policy purchase and early retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business goals into a portfolio of bets, balancing big swings that get signal quickly with disciplined follow-ups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence in experimentation on lower-traffic, high-value surfaces: fast kill-or-continue decisions, clean sequencing, and careful management of interacting tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering, Design, and Analytics, and collaborate with Underwriting, Sales, and Compliance to create innovative solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the product function on complex cross-functional tradeoffs involving underwriting risk, operational cost, and conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate strategy, results, and learnings clearly to executive leadership and the broader organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the user in every forum: advocate for experiences that are accessible, delightful, and simple&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product management experience at high-growth technology companies, building consumer products at significant scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years managing and developing product managers, including managers or senior ICs, with a track record of building high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience owning conversion in complex, high-consideration purchase flows, ideally from application or checkout through purchase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of running rigorous A/B testing programs, including on lower-traffic surfaces where speed of decision-making matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, insurtech, healthcare, or other regulated consumer industries, and comfort partnering with risk, operations, and compliance teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with personalization or ML-driven recommendations is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong UX instincts and storytelling: you know how to explain complex financial decisions simply and help users feel confident&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical orientation; proficient with SQL, Hex, Mixpanel, Amplitude (or similar) for self-serve analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication clear reasoning; able to influence across functions and levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating at multiple altitudes, from multi-year vision to hands-on execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
