&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ethos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethos (Nasdaq: $LIFE) &lt;/strong&gt;is a leading life insurance technology company on a mission to protect families by democratizing access to life insurance and empowering agents at scale. With its robust three-sided technology platform, Ethos is transforming the life insurance experience for consumers, agents, and carriers alike. Ethos offers instant, accessible products and a seamless online process that requires no medical exams and just a few health questions; it eliminates traditional barriers, making it easier than ever for everyone to protect their families. Ethos is redefining how life insurance is bought, sold, and underwritten.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a data-obsessed, US-based Senior Growth Marketing Manager to own the lifecycle across three distinct customer journeys: converting prospects into customers, expanding existing customers through cross-sell and upsell, and scaling a recently launched product line. The through-line is conversion, retention, and maximizing long-term customer value (LTV).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These three journeys work differently, and that&#39;s the interesting part of the job. Prospect-to-customer conversion is a blend of self-serve digital and human follow-up — live agents and voice AI — so your job is to design what gets said, to whom, and when, so that confidence keeps building in the gaps between conversations. Cross-sell, upsell, and the new product line are entirely self-serve. There is no human in the loop, which means the messaging, the timing, and the on-page experience have to carry the entire decision on their own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Life insurance is a high-consideration purchase, so lack of trust and product understanding are the biggest drivers of drop-off. Across all three journeys, you own the connective tissue that moves someone from &quot;a company I found on the internet&quot; to &quot;a company I trust to safeguard my future.&quot; You will operate on shared OKRs with the product managers who own each of these three areas, and — for the conversion journey — in close working partnership with Sales leadership, agents, and our voice AI team. You need to know what&#39;s actually landing on live calls, not just what performs in an inbox.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Lifecycle Strategy and Messaging. &lt;/strong&gt;Design the narrative, cadence, and channel mix that carries someone from first touch to funded policy, from first policy to second, and from early interest in a new product line to scaled adoption. You set the strategy and you build it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Convert Prospects into Customers. &lt;/strong&gt;Own the post-lead journey where self-serve and human touch meet. Build the digital nurture that moves people forward on their own, and build the follow-up content, sequences, and talking points that make every agent and voice AI conversation land — the right articles, proof points, or next steps that can go out within minutes of a call ending, and a system that gets smarter over time rather than sending the same packet to everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Cross-Sell and Upsell. &lt;/strong&gt;Existing customers are our highest-intent audience and this motion is fully self-serve. Own identifying the right next product for the right customer at the right moment — additional coverage, product upgrades, a second policy for a spouse — and build the triggered messaging, on-page experiences, and offer structures that get them there without a human touch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale a Recently Launched Product Line. &lt;/strong&gt;We have a new product line in market and the mandate is growth. Own its self-serve lifecycle end to end: activation, onboarding, and the messaging that turns early traction into a repeatable, scaling funnel. This is 0→1 becoming 1→10, with the ambiguity and speed that implies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Retention and LTV. &lt;/strong&gt;Getting someone to buy is the beginning, not the end. Own the post-purchase journey that keeps policies in force and customers engaged, and be accountable for LTV as a number you move, not a metric you report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Trust Signals Across the Funnel. &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with Marketing and Product on the things that actually move a high-consideration financial decision: credibility and social proof, carrier proof points, reviews, and transparency about what someone is actually buying.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Data Behind Conversion and Drop-Off. &lt;/strong&gt;Be the expert on cohorts and funnel curves across all three areas. Pull your own data to find exactly where trust and momentum break down, not just where a campaign underperforms — then turn that into a concrete hypothesis and test it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run Experiments End to End. &lt;/strong&gt;Test messaging, cadence, offers, and channel mix; report on statistical significance; roll out what wins.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Ownership. &lt;/strong&gt;Operate on shared OKRs with the product managers across all three areas, and in a real working relationship with Sales leadership on the conversion journey. Decisions get made, ownership is felt, and campaigns don&#39;t stall because nobody knows who&#39;s driving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope. &lt;/strong&gt;Your time splits across all three journeys with the weighting shifting as each area matures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6+ Years of Experience. &lt;/strong&gt;Senior-level track record in Lifecycle, Growth Marketing, or CRM at a B2C Tech, FinTech, Insurtech, or Marketplace company. Higher-consideration / higher-AOV product experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Copywriting and Messaging Strategy. &lt;/strong&gt;You can write subject lines that get opened and body copy that drives action — and you know how to build trust and clarity into a high-consideration financial decision, not just optimize for clicks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-Serve Conversion Instincts. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ve moved customers through a purchase decision with no human in the loop and you know what that demands: the messaging, the timing, and the on-page experience all have to do the persuading.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable Partnering with a Sales Org. &lt;/strong&gt;For the conversion journey, you want to know what&#39;s actually said on a live call, and you can translate that into content and tools that make agents and voice AI more effective — not assets built in isolation from what&#39;s happening in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-Channel Mindset. &lt;/strong&gt;You think natively across email, SMS, voice / conversational AI, in-product, on-page, and human-delivered follow-up. You do not believe email is the center of the universe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Mindset. &lt;/strong&gt;Fluent in cohort retention, statistical significance, and LTV. Ability to self service data pulls/queries to find where trust and momentum break down in the funnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical CRM Proficiency. &lt;/strong&gt;Hands-on expertise with enterprise marketing automation tools (e.g., Braze, Iterable, Customer.io, HubSpot, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PM Collaboration. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ve worked on a shared goal / OKR with a PM before and have a strong sense of when to lead, when to follow, and how to drive decisions across a cross-functional team. Here you&#39;ll do it with several PMs at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
