&lt;p&gt;Ethos is a life insurance technology company on a mission to protect the next million families. Our platform serves consumers, agents, and carriers, and it turns a process that used to take weeks into one that takes minutes. We&#39;re a team that cares deeply, thinks clearly, and moves fast, with real ownership and very little red tape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; As a Senior Technical Program Manager, you&#39;ll lead cross-team programs that move the business forward, from carrier integrations and partner launches to internal tooling and platform improvements. You&#39;ll bring structure to ambiguity, keep many teams pulling in the same direction, and make sure what we ship is what we meant to ship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end delivery of cross-functional programs, from scoping and planning through launch and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-impact programs end to end with minimal oversight, owning the outcome rather than just the plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Product, Data, Operations, and external partners to turn goals into clear plans, milestones, and owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot risks and dependencies early, raise them plainly, and drive decisions instead of waiting on consensus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep program health visible with crisp written updates, so leaders and teams always know where things stand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dig into technical details (architecture, integrations, data flows) well enough to ask the right questions and make good tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run retrospectives after every launch and feed what you learn back into how we plan and execute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical program management (or similar) at a technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of delivering complex programs that span multiple engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough technical depth to engage with engineers on system design, APIs, and integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, including with senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity, and the judgment to prioritize and adjust quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven approach: you define success metrics up front and measure against them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in insurance, fintech, or another regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with partner or third-party integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to speed up planning, reporting, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
